  "question": "A battery of emf $E$ and internal resistance $r$ delivers maximum power to an external resistor $R$ when",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$R = r$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$R = 2r$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$R = \\dfrac{r}{2}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$R \\to \\infty$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$P = \\dfrac{E^2R}{(R + r)^2}$ is maximum when $\\dfrac{dP}{dR} = 0$, which gives $R = r$. Then $P_{max} = \\dfrac{E^2}{4r}$.",
